WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.700
- My next guest is one of
the hottest WWE superstars

00:00:03.700 --> 00:00:04.930
on the planet.

00:00:04.930 --> 00:00:07.750
In January, she made history
as the second black person

00:00:07.750 --> 00:00:09.260
to win the Royal Rumble.

00:00:09.260 --> 00:00:11.040
Who was the first you may ask?

00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:13.560
Well, just a little known
wrestler by the name of The Rock,

00:00:13.560 --> 00:00:16.350
not bad footsteps to follow in.

00:00:16.350 --> 00:00:18.901
That's why we call her
a whole lotta woman.

00:00:18.901 --> 00:00:21.484
(upbeat music)

00:00:22.870 --> 00:00:26.350
All right, she's known
as the EST of the WWE.

00:00:26.350 --> 00:00:29.513
Please, welcome WWE
Superstar, Bianca Belair.

00:00:30.492 --> 00:00:33.075
(upbeat music)

00:00:34.540 --> 00:00:36.338
Woo, first of all-

00:00:36.338 --> 00:00:37.171
- Hi.

00:00:37.171 --> 00:00:38.510
- Wait, I love the room you're in

00:00:38.510 --> 00:00:41.670
with the black and gold,
that's so Gatsby, I love it.

00:00:41.670 --> 00:00:42.930
That's super cool.

00:00:42.930 --> 00:00:43.763
- Thank you.

00:00:43.763 --> 00:00:44.596
- [Kerry] Yes.

00:00:44.596 --> 00:00:45.429
- Thank you.

00:00:45.429 --> 00:00:47.200
- Well, and also, I have to ask you,

00:00:47.200 --> 00:00:49.810
what does the EST of the WWE?

00:00:49.810 --> 00:00:50.643
What does that mean?

00:00:50.643 --> 00:00:51.650
What does that stand for?

00:00:51.650 --> 00:00:53.870
- I call myself the EST of WWE.

00:00:53.870 --> 00:00:56.680
It basically means that I'm the strongest,

00:00:56.680 --> 00:00:58.100
I'm the fastest, I'm the roughest,

00:00:58.100 --> 00:00:59.180
I'm the toughest, I'm the quickest,

00:00:59.180 --> 00:01:00.390
I'm the greatest, I'm the best.

00:01:00.390 --> 00:01:04.090
The B-E-S-T is anything
good that ends in E-S-T.

00:01:04.090 --> 00:01:06.280
Now I've played sports
my whole entire life.

00:01:06.280 --> 00:01:08.780
And I was a collegiate hurdler

00:01:08.780 --> 00:01:10.160
at the University of Tennessee.

00:01:10.160 --> 00:01:12.307
And afterwards, I went into CrossFit

00:01:12.307 --> 00:01:14.530
and I made my own gear
and I really stood out.

00:01:14.530 --> 00:01:17.870
So I was contacted by Mark
Henry, who is a Hall of Famer.

00:01:17.870 --> 00:01:20.440
And he asked me if I ever
thought of being a WWE wrestler.

00:01:20.440 --> 00:01:22.370
And he told me just be myself.

00:01:22.370 --> 00:01:26.750
I went through two tryouts and
I got hired in April of 2016.

00:01:26.750 --> 00:01:28.770
- Oh my gosh, just like listening to you.

00:01:28.770 --> 00:01:29.700
(audience clapping)

00:01:29.700 --> 00:01:33.380
We're so much alike (laughs)

00:01:33.380 --> 00:01:35.300
So so similar.

00:01:35.300 --> 00:01:38.030
You're so athletic, good Lord.

00:01:38.030 --> 00:01:40.040
So you're known for your long braid,

00:01:40.040 --> 00:01:41.720
which is fabulous by the way,

00:01:41.720 --> 00:01:44.630
we even have video of
you jump roping with it.

00:01:44.630 --> 00:01:46.740
So do you use it in the ring?

00:01:46.740 --> 00:01:47.660
It's amazing.

00:01:47.660 --> 00:01:51.130
- Oh yes, I definitely use it.

00:01:51.130 --> 00:01:52.740
At first, it was just a signature look

00:01:52.740 --> 00:01:54.790
so that I could stand out and be unique.

00:01:54.790 --> 00:01:57.870
And I had a match where I
threw it at one of the girls

00:01:57.870 --> 00:02:00.320
and it made this huge noise
and the crowd reacted.

00:02:00.320 --> 00:02:01.907
And I was like, what was that?

00:02:01.907 --> 00:02:02.970
Was that my hair?

00:02:02.970 --> 00:02:04.100
And that's when I realized,

00:02:04.100 --> 00:02:06.380
oh, this is not just a signature look,

00:02:06.380 --> 00:02:07.900
this can be used as a weapon.

00:02:07.900 --> 00:02:12.310
So, I definitely use this as
my secret weapon in the ring.

00:02:12.310 --> 00:02:13.650
- I already see the movie

00:02:13.650 --> 00:02:16.640
and you're like some kind of really cool,

00:02:16.640 --> 00:02:17.473
I don't know,

00:02:17.473 --> 00:02:18.830
you're saving the day and
you're using your hair

00:02:18.830 --> 00:02:20.340
and you're just kicking ass with it.

00:02:20.340 --> 00:02:21.420
I don't know, I see it.

00:02:21.420 --> 00:02:24.410
I'm just saying, are your
parents your biggest fans

00:02:24.410 --> 00:02:26.717
or did they get worried
with just all of that?

00:02:26.717 --> 00:02:30.300
- Oh, my parents have been
there every step of the way.

00:02:30.300 --> 00:02:33.330
They always support me even with track

00:02:33.330 --> 00:02:34.660
and gymnastics and CrossFit,

00:02:34.660 --> 00:02:35.970
anything that I do, they support me.

00:02:35.970 --> 00:02:38.360
So when it came to being in the WWE,

00:02:38.360 --> 00:02:40.090
they have completely fallen in love.

00:02:40.090 --> 00:02:41.870
My dad gets very crazy.

00:02:41.870 --> 00:02:42.703
He gets excited.

00:02:42.703 --> 00:02:44.560
He falls over the back of the couch

00:02:44.560 --> 00:02:46.640
because he gets so excited
every time I come out,

00:02:46.640 --> 00:02:49.500
even if it's my entrance
and nobody ever believes me,

00:02:49.500 --> 00:02:51.650
but my mom gets amped up.

00:02:51.650 --> 00:02:53.160
They're my biggest fans.

00:02:53.160 --> 00:02:54.660
And I just love them so much.

00:02:54.660 --> 00:02:57.820
And it's amazing to
have parents like them.

00:02:57.820 --> 00:02:59.070
I'm just super blessed.

00:02:59.070 --> 00:03:02.070
- Well, we actually have
video of Bianca's parents

00:03:02.070 --> 00:03:04.419
watching her from home, so take a look.

00:03:04.419 --> 00:03:07.370
(air whooshing)

00:03:07.370 --> 00:03:10.453
(cheering excitedly)

00:03:15.080 --> 00:03:17.830
- [Bianca's Dad] Yeah, baby, woo!

00:03:23.182 --> 00:03:26.196
- [Bianca's Mom] Oh,
wow, point to the sun,

00:03:26.196 --> 00:03:27.897
point to the sun.

00:03:27.897 --> 00:03:29.954
(laughing)

00:03:29.954 --> 00:03:31.613
- I would watch that show.

00:03:33.660 --> 00:03:35.730
Oh my gosh, it's amazing.

00:03:35.730 --> 00:03:37.340
They are amped.

00:03:37.340 --> 00:03:39.143
It's like they're there with you.

00:03:40.100 --> 00:03:43.680
- Yes, it gives me, I get
so excited watching them

00:03:43.680 --> 00:03:45.901
and I love that they can
be a part of this with me.

00:03:45.901 --> 00:03:48.080
I'm tearing up now just watching it,

00:03:48.080 --> 00:03:52.011
but they are the best parents
that I could ever ask for.

00:03:52.011 --> 00:03:54.520
- That really is a beautiful thing.

00:03:54.520 --> 00:03:56.420
Well, Wrestle Mania is this weekend.

00:03:56.420 --> 00:03:59.380
So, what makes this year
so significant, you think?

00:03:59.380 --> 00:04:00.740
- Well, for me,

00:04:00.740 --> 00:04:04.930
this will be my first
Wrestle Mania title match,

00:04:04.930 --> 00:04:07.030
and I'm actually going
up against Sasha Banks

00:04:07.030 --> 00:04:09.170
who is the Smack Down Women's Champion.

00:04:09.170 --> 00:04:11.860
And we are actually creating
history on this night.

00:04:11.860 --> 00:04:14.470
It'll be the first time that
two African-American women

00:04:14.470 --> 00:04:16.880
are having a title match at Wrestle Mania.

00:04:16.880 --> 00:04:18.180
So we're gonna be in the greatest thing

00:04:18.180 --> 00:04:19.876
of all creating history.

00:04:19.876 --> 00:04:20.760
(audience clapping)

00:04:20.760 --> 00:04:23.153
It's also gonna be two nights.

00:04:24.310 --> 00:04:26.400
It'll be on April 10th and April 11th

00:04:26.400 --> 00:04:28.120
at Raymond James Stadium in Tampa Bay.

00:04:28.120 --> 00:04:28.980
It'll be the first time

00:04:28.980 --> 00:04:31.860
that we're having fans back in a year.

00:04:31.860 --> 00:04:34.340
We're gonna be on Peacock.

00:04:34.340 --> 00:04:36.220
It'll be the first time that
Wrestle Mania be on Peacock.

00:04:36.220 --> 00:04:38.630
It's the new home of the WWE Network.

00:04:38.630 --> 00:04:41.090
We're gonna have 25,000 fans.

00:04:41.090 --> 00:04:43.120
We're following all safety protocols.

00:04:43.120 --> 00:04:45.520
We're having pods,
we're social distancing.

00:04:45.520 --> 00:04:48.000
They're doing temperature
checks, masks are required.

00:04:48.000 --> 00:04:51.480
And we just really been doing
a lot of PSA announcements

00:04:51.480 --> 00:04:53.160
about COVID and vaccinations

00:04:53.160 --> 00:04:55.420
and everyone's super excited
to get back to normal.

00:04:55.420 --> 00:04:56.490
And I think the first step

00:04:56.490 --> 00:04:58.450
is everyone rolling up their
sleeves, doing their part,

00:04:58.450 --> 00:05:00.860
getting vaccinated so that
we can get back to normal.

00:05:00.860 --> 00:05:02.960
And I think we're jump-starting

00:05:02.960 --> 00:05:07.710
that with having a two night
Wrestle Mania with 25,000 fans.

00:05:07.710 --> 00:05:10.150
It's gonna feel like a family reunion

00:05:10.150 --> 00:05:12.680
in having our fans back and
being able to create history

00:05:12.680 --> 00:05:14.950
in front of our fans with Sasha Banks.

00:05:14.950 --> 00:05:17.080
And I'll be going for the Smack
Down Women's Championship.

00:05:17.080 --> 00:05:18.930
And hopefully, I'll be walking out

00:05:18.930 --> 00:05:21.790
as the new champion at Wrestle Mania.

00:05:21.790 --> 00:05:26.440
- Okay, well, here's the
thing, I need the video

00:05:26.440 --> 00:05:29.960
of your parents watching
you win that (laughs)

00:05:29.960 --> 00:05:33.560
'cause I feel like what you're gonna do

00:05:33.560 --> 00:05:37.570
is gonna be nothing in
comparison to how crazy they get.

00:05:37.570 --> 00:05:40.550
They're gonna be so excited, (laughs)

00:05:40.550 --> 00:05:41.590
- Probably gonna pass out,

00:05:41.590 --> 00:05:44.000
we're gonna need to carry
them out on a stretcher.

00:05:44.000 --> 00:05:46.990
- I know, he's already
falling off couches.

00:05:46.990 --> 00:05:49.280
Well, you're also, I think
this is really cool too

00:05:49.280 --> 00:05:52.410
because when you have this kind of power,

00:05:52.410 --> 00:05:53.420
this kind of spotlight,

00:05:53.420 --> 00:05:55.810
it's really cool that you
use it for other things,

00:05:55.810 --> 00:05:56.720
not just for oneself.

00:05:56.720 --> 00:05:59.640
So you're also involved in
a program called Girl Up.

00:05:59.640 --> 00:06:01.090
So, can you tell us about it?

00:06:01.090 --> 00:06:03.380
- Yes, it's amazing.

00:06:03.380 --> 00:06:05.340
WWE and Girl Up, they partner together

00:06:05.340 --> 00:06:07.710
to promote gender equity in sports.

00:06:07.710 --> 00:06:11.720
And WWE has launched the
Girl Up scholarship fund

00:06:11.720 --> 00:06:13.330
where they provide scholarships

00:06:13.330 --> 00:06:15.150
for 10 girls around the world.

00:06:15.150 --> 00:06:17.610
And it's just super important
to encourage young girls

00:06:17.610 --> 00:06:19.050
to get into sports and stay in sports

00:06:19.050 --> 00:06:21.700
because it just promotes
so many great qualities.

00:06:21.700 --> 00:06:25.440
And I play sports all throughout
my life since I was five.

00:06:25.440 --> 00:06:27.438
And I really feel like
it's really contributed

00:06:27.438 --> 00:06:30.350
to the success that
I'm experiencing today.

00:06:30.350 --> 00:06:33.610
And so, WWE, Girl Up, and
also Sports For Purpose

00:06:33.610 --> 00:06:35.270
which is another program that we have,

00:06:35.270 --> 00:06:37.140
we just wanna make sure that
we're providing the resources

00:06:37.140 --> 00:06:39.700
and the opportunities and the
information to young girls

00:06:39.700 --> 00:06:42.580
to encourage them to get into
sports and stay in sports.

00:06:42.580 --> 00:06:45.980
And we're providing these
spaces to have conversations.

00:06:45.980 --> 00:06:47.240
These must be the conversations

00:06:47.240 --> 00:06:49.570
which we do by having
panels with a female coach

00:06:49.570 --> 00:06:50.960
which I've been a part of.

00:06:50.960 --> 00:06:52.860
And we're just talking
about the importance

00:06:52.860 --> 00:06:55.100
of girls getting in
sports and also talking

00:06:55.100 --> 00:06:58.580
about the importance of
representation of females in sports.

00:06:58.580 --> 00:07:01.730
So it's amazing things that
WWE and Girl Up are doing.

00:07:01.730 --> 00:07:03.640
I'm so happy to be a part of it.

00:07:03.640 --> 00:07:05.053
- Absolutely, absolutely.

